cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, the annotations, or the findings below, please cite it."
title: "Long-tailed dental radiograph detection and instance segmentation"
abstract: >-
  Detection and instance segmentation on a 31-class panoramic dental radiograph
  corpus with extreme class imbalance. Contains a data-integrity toolchain that
  identifies and corrects a 95.9% train/test contamination in the source
  release, long-tail, boundary-aware and input-resolution modifications to both
  architectures, frozen ablation matrices attributing each change to a single
  component, and a shared evaluation stack covering COCO metrics, contour
  metrics, a clinical endpoint and bootstrap confidence intervals.
authors:
